/target
/.pact
# Any workspace's own derived area, not only this repository's. A `watch/`
# document writes its record to `<workspace>/.pact/watch/`, so running the
# worked example leaves one under `examples/refund-desk/`. D2 says deleting a
# `.pact/` must be harmless; committing one would make that untrue.
.pact/
/research/repos
/research/papers/*.pdf
# The TypeScript port's installed dependencies and its build cache. `tsc` is a
# devDependency so `scripts/test-all.sh` can type-check the second port at all;
# what it installs is not source.
/adapters/typescript/node_modules

# mkdocs output. `site-docs/` is the source; `site/` is generated.
/site

# Python build and tool caches. The repo has no commits yet, so without these
# the first `git add` would capture every one of them.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.deepeval/
*.log

# Claude Code's own session directory — agent definitions, workflow scripts and
# a scheduler lock. Tooling used to WORK on PACT, not part of PACT.
/.claude

# One-off HTML reports generated while reviewing. `docs/` is where a finding
# that matters is written down; a rendered copy of one is not source.
/site-report
